      severity: "low"  # 04f7
      statement: "Among 84 AnalysisRun records, 83 carry version='5.0.1' (the project's semver) and 1 (play-routes) carries version='1'. Both runs have identical toolchain={'name': 'python', 'version': '3.12.3'}. The version field carries two different value scales — semver vs single-digit revision. Either play-routes was developed against a v1 schema-version stamp and never updated to track the project version, OR the version field has different semantics per analyzer (semver for project, internal-revision for analyzers). Either way the same field carries two scales without schema-level distinction."  # 04f7
      root_cause: "play-routes analyzer emits version='1' independently of the project semver injection. No central version-stamping policy enforces consistency across analyzers. Same family as pass-19 AAAAAAAA (canonical_name dual-format): one field, two formats."  # 04f7
